// A term holds one payload inline, the way an option does, so converting one
// is the same shape of work and there is no reason it could not be done. There
// is just no arm for it in the runtime's walk, and admitting it without one
// would mean two descriptors of different sizes reaching the arm that copies,
// which refuses rather than corrupts but refuses at run time.
//
// The call below reports F002 as well, because a signature that does not
// resolve leaves its function unregistered. That one used to be the only thing
// said, which named the symptom and left the reader to guess.
fun f<T>(x: term Wrapped T): bool
  ret true
end fun

let output = f(term Wrapped 1)
